[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Intertube.Stub project, examples and samples requirements
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: intertube.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document covers everything about Intertube.Stub that is not library behaviour: how the
package is built and published (PKG), the continuous integration pipeline (CI), the repository
documentation (DOC), the example systems under test in examples/ (EX), the RedisLite sample
application in samples/ (RL), and the overall verification strategy (VER). The library's own
behaviour (core servers, SMTP and SFTP) is specified in the other documents in this folder.

The key words "shall", "should" and "may" carry the meaning given to them by RFC 2119.

VERIFIED_BY lists how each requirement is checked. A line of the form "- Type.Member" names an
automated test: Type is the C# test class (without namespace) or the last segment of the F#
module name, and Member is the C# method name or the text between double backticks of the F#
test. A line of the form "- Review: path" means the requirement is checked by reading that file.
RequirementsTraceTests fails the build if any named test does not exist.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Packaging

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Package identity
STATEMENT: >>>
The library project src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj shall produce a NuGet package with
PackageId Intertube.Stub and Version 0.1.0-preview.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A prerelease version signals that the public API may still change before the first release.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Target frameworks
STATEMENT: >>>
The library shall target net8.0 and net10.0, and shall reference System.IO.Pipelines 8.0.0 only
for the net8.0 target.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: MIT licence expression
STATEMENT: >>>
The package shall declare its licence with PackageLicenseExpression MIT, and the repository
shall contain a LICENSE file with the MIT licence text and the copyright line
"Copyright (c) 2026 Jeff Dickson".
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
- Review: LICENSE
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Package metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
The package shall declare Authors, Copyright, Description, PackageTags, PackageProjectUrl,
RepositoryUrl and RepositoryType git, with the project and repository URLs pointing at
https://github.com/jeffadickson/Intertube.Stub.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: README shipped in the package
STATEMENT: >>>
The package shall include the repository's README.md at the package root and name it as
PackageReadmeFile, so that nuget.org shows it as the package description page.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Symbol package
STATEMENT: >>>
Packing the library shall also produce a symbol package in the snupkg format (IncludeSymbols true,
SymbolPackageFormat snupkg).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SourceLink
STATEMENT: >>>
The library shall be built with SourceLink information: PublishRepositoryUrl and
EmbedUntrackedSources shall be true, relying on the SourceLink support built into the .NET 8+
SDK for GitHub.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Deterministic CI builds
STATEMENT: >>>
ContinuousIntegrationBuild shall be set to true when the build runs on GitHub Actions
(GITHUB_ACTIONS is true), and only then.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deterministic paths in the PDBs are needed for reproducible packages but hinder local debugging.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Package validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The library project shall set EnablePackageValidation to true, so that pack checks the package
for inconsistencies between its target frameworks.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AOT compatibility analysis
STATEMENT: >>>
The library shall set IsAotCompatible to true for every target framework compatible with net8.0,
so that trimming and native AOT analyzers run during the build.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: XML documentation
STATEMENT: >>>
The library shall generate an XML documentation file that ships in the package. The missing-doc
warning CS1591 may be suppressed.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Nullable reference types
STATEMENT: >>>
The library shall be compiled with nullable reference types enabled and the latest C# language
version.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Warnings as errors
STATEMENT: >>>
The build of the whole solution shall treat every compiler and analyzer warning as an error.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
- Review: CONTRIBUTING.md
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
This is enforced by the -warnaserror switch in CI and in the documented local build command, not
by a TreatWarningsAsErrors property in the library project. There is no Directory.Build.props.
Only samples/RedisLite/RedisLite.csproj sets TreatWarningsAsErrors itself.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Internals visible only to the test project
STATEMENT: >>>
The library shall expose its internals only to the Intertube.Stub.Tests assembly.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Only the library is packable
STATEMENT: >>>
Every test, example and sample test project shall set IsPackable to false, so that packing the
solution produces only the Intertube.Stub package.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: tests/Intertube.Stub.Tests/Intertube.Stub.Tests.csproj
- Review: examples/Intertube.Stub.Examples/Intertube.Stub.Examples.csproj
- Review: examples/Intertube.Stub.FSharp/Intertube.Stub.FSharp.fsproj
- Review: samples/RedisLite.Tests/RedisLite.Tests.csproj
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-016
STATUS: Deferred
TITLE: Release notes in the package
STATEMENT: >>>
The package should carry PackageReleaseNotes describing the changes in each version.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deferred by the maintainer until the first release.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-017
STATUS: Deferred
TITLE: Package icon
STATEMENT: >>>
The package should include an icon referenced by PackageIcon.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deferred by the maintainer until the first release.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-PKG-018
STATUS: Deferred
TITLE: Public API baseline
STATEMENT: >>>
The library should use Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers with PublicAPI.Shipped.txt and
PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt baseline files, so that every change to the public API is deliberate.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deferred by the maintainer until the first release.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Build and continuous integration

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Triggers
STATEMENT: >>>
The CI workflow shall run on every push to main and on every pull request.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Operating system matrix
STATEMENT: >>>
The CI test job shall run on ubuntu-latest, windows-latest and macos-latest, with fail-fast
disabled so that a failure on one operating system does not cancel the others.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Socket behaviour (resets, Unix socket paths, timing) differs between platforms.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Read-only token
STATEMENT: >>>
The workflow shall grant the GITHUB_TOKEN only contents: read permission.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Concurrency
STATEMENT: >>>
The workflow shall group runs by workflow and ref and cancel an in-progress run when a newer run
for the same ref starts.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Job timeout
STATEMENT: >>>
Each CI test job shall time out after 20 minutes.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Both SDKs installed
STATEMENT: >>>
The CI job shall install the .NET 8.0.x and 10.0.x SDKs, with .NET CLI telemetry and the logo
banner turned off.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Release build with warnings as errors
STATEMENT: >>>
CI shall build Intertube.slnx in the Release configuration with -warnaserror.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Tests with hang detection
STATEMENT: >>>
CI shall run every test project in the solution in Release without rebuilding, with a blame hang
timeout of 5 minutes and normal console verbosity.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A hung network test then produces a dump and a named culprit instead of hitting the job timeout.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Pack and upload the package
STATEMENT: >>>
On ubuntu-latest only, CI shall pack src/Intertube.Stub in Release without rebuilding, and upload
the .nupkg and .snupkg as an artifact named package-(commit SHA), failing if no file is found.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Actions pinned to commit SHAs
STATEMENT: >>>
Every third-party action used by the workflow shall be pinned to a full commit SHA, with the
version tag recorded in a trailing comment.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/workflows/ci.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dependabot
STATEMENT: >>>
Dependabot shall check the github-actions and nuget ecosystems of the repository root weekly.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: .github/dependabot.yml
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: OpenSSH interop tests required on CI
STATEMENT: >>>
The OpenSSH interop tests shall be skipped when sftp and ssh-keygen are not on the PATH, except
when the CI environment variable is "true" or "True", in which case they shall run and fail
rather than be skipped.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A runner image that lost OpenSSH must not silently turn the interop coverage green.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: tests/Intertube.Stub.Tests/Sftp/OpenSsh.cs
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Pinned local tools
STATEMENT: >>>
The repository shall declare dotnet-stryker as a local tool in dotnet-tools.json at an exact
version (4.16.0) with roll-forward disabled.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: dotnet-tools.json
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CI-014
STATUS: Deferred
TITLE: Release job publishing to NuGet
STATEMENT: >>>
A release workflow should publish the package and symbol package to nuget.org from a tagged
commit.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deferred by the maintainer until the first release.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Documentation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: README install section
STATEMENT: >>>
README.md shall contain an Install section giving the command
"dotnet add package Intertube.Stub --prerelease", naming the Intertube.Stub,
Intertube.Stub.Smtp and Intertube.Stub.Sftp namespaces and the supported target frameworks.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: README.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: README links are absolute
STATEMENT: >>>
Every link in README.md shall be an absolute https URL, so that the links keep working when the
README is rendered on nuget.org from inside the package.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: README.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: README loopback warning
STATEMENT: >>>
README.md shall warn, in its SFTP section, that SftpServer binds 127.0.0.1 by default, that the
address shall not be changed to a non-loopback address, and why: with no Users configured any
login is accepted, so a DirectorySftpFileSystem would be readable and writable by anyone who
can reach the port.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: README.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: README feature overview and usage
STATEMENT: >>>
README.md shall describe, with code samples, the transports, framing helpers, lifecycle,
concurrency, transcripts and assertions, scripted conversations, rule tables, fault injection,
UDP, Unix sockets and the ready-made SFTP and SMTP servers.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: README.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: README states the test-double limits
STATEMENT: >>>
README.md shall state that the SFTP server is not a production server: no rate limiting, no
privilege separation, and Ed25519 verification that is not constant-time.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: README.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: README layout, licence and policy links
STATEMENT: >>>
README.md shall describe the repository layout (src, tests, examples, samples), state the MIT
licence and link to LICENSE, SECURITY.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, examples/README.md and
samples/README.md.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: README.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: README CI badge
STATEMENT: >>>
README.md should show the status badge of the CI workflow.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: README.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Private vulnerability reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
SECURITY.md shall direct reporters to GitHub Security Advisories for the repository, ask them not
to open public issues for security problems, and ask for the version, target framework and a
minimal reproduction.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: SECURITY.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Security scope
STATEMENT: >>>
SECURITY.md shall define the library as a loopback test double, list what is in scope (crashing
or hanging the test host, escaping a DirectorySftpFileSystem root, a default exposing a server
beyond loopback) and state that production-only weaknesses such as denial of service under load
and timing side channels are generally out of scope.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: SECURITY.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Security loopback guidance
STATEMENT: >>>
SECURITY.md shall state that every server binds 127.0.0.1 by default and that a non-loopback
address shall never be bound on a machine reachable by untrusted parties, singling out
SftpServer, SmtpServer and file-touching TcpServer handlers.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: SECURITY.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Contributor prerequisites
STATEMENT: >>>
CONTRIBUTING.md shall list the prerequisites: the .NET 10 SDK plus the .NET 8 runtime, and an
OpenSSH client (sftp and ssh-keygen on the PATH) for the SFTP interop tests, explaining that
those tests are skipped locally without it.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: CONTRIBUTING.md
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
CONTRIBUTING.md does not mention that the interop tests fail instead of skipping when CI=true
(ITS-CI-012).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Contributor build and test commands
STATEMENT: >>>
CONTRIBUTING.md shall give the build command with -warnaserror and the test command, and state
how CI differs (Release configuration, packing with dotnet pack).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: CONTRIBUTING.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Pull request rules
STATEMENT: >>>
CONTRIBUTING.md shall require pull requests to build without warnings, to pass on all three CI
operating systems and both target frameworks, to avoid timing- and OS-error-code-dependent
tests, to add tests for behaviour changes and to update README.md when the public API changes.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: CONTRIBUTING.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Examples index
STATEMENT: >>>
examples/README.md shall list every example file with the dependency it mocks and the
Intertube.Stub features it shows, describe the F# project, and give the command to run the
examples.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: examples/README.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Samples guide
STATEMENT: >>>
samples/README.md shall describe the RedisLite projects, the design points under test, how
FakeRedis uses each Intertube.Stub feature, the FsCheck and Hedgehog properties, and how to run
Stryker with the recorded mutation scores.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: samples/README.md
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-DOC-016
STATUS: Deferred
TITLE: Changelog
STATEMENT: >>>
The repository should contain a CHANGELOG recording the user-visible changes of each release.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deferred by the maintainer until the first release.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Examples

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Each example is a small, realistic system under test that uses ordinary .NET networking and knows
nothing about Intertube.Stub, together with the tests that mock its network dependency. The
requirements below state what each example shall demonstrate.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DNS resolver
STATEMENT: >>>
The DNS example shall demonstrate a resolver against a fake authoritative name server serving UDP
and TCP on the same port: A records over UDP without opening TCP, CNAME chains followed, NXDOMAIN
reported and not retried, a truncated (TC) answer retried over TCP, packet loss ridden out with
retries, SERVFAIL and a silent primary failing over to the secondary, a spoofed reply with the
wrong ID ignored, and giving up with a timeout when every server is silent.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- DnsExample.ResolvesARecords_OverUdp
- DnsExample.FollowsCnameChains
- DnsExample.NxDomain_IsReportedAsSuch_AndNotRetried
- DnsExample.TruncatedAnswer_IsRetriedOverTcp
- DnsExample.PacketLoss_IsRiddenOutWithRetries
- DnsExample.ServFail_MovesOnToTheNextServer
- DnsExample.SilentPrimary_TimesOut_ThenTheSecondaryAnswers
- DnsExample.SpoofedReplyWithTheWrongId_IsIgnored
- DnsExample.EveryServerSilent_GivesUp
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Docker over a Unix socket
STATEMENT: >>>
The Docker example shall demonstrate HTTP over a UnixServer at a temporary path, reached through
SocketsHttpHandler.ConnectCallback: listing only running containers, and a restart posted to the
right endpoint, with an error status surfacing as HttpRequestException.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- DockerUnixSocketExample.ListsOnlyRunningContainers
- DockerUnixSocketExample.Restart_PostsToTheRightEndpoint
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: FTPS file exchange
STATEMENT: >>>
The FTP example shall demonstrate a FluentFTP client against a fake FTPS server built on the SFTP
in-memory file system, with explicit TLS on control and data connections: an encrypted upload
verified then renamed, download then delete, a one-off disk-full failure retried, a server that
silently truncates uploads caught by a SIZE check, a data connection dropped mid-download
reported as an error rather than a truncated file, a server without TLS refused rather than
downgraded, an impostor certificate rejected, and a wrong password not retried.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FtpExample.Upload_IsEncryptedEndToEnd_VerifiedThenRenamed
- FtpExample.Collect_DownloadsThenDeletes
- FtpExample.DiskFullOnce_IsRetried
- FtpExample.ServerThatSilentlyTruncatesUploads_IsCaughtBySizeCheck
- FtpExample.DataConnectionDroppedMidDownload_IsAnError_NotATruncatedFile
- FtpExample.ServerWithoutTls_IsRefused_NotDowngraded
- FtpExample.ImpostorCertificate_IsRejected
- FtpExample.WrongPassword_IsNotRetried
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: HL7 MLLP sender
STATEMENT: >>>
The HL7 example shall demonstrate an MLLP sender against a fake receiver that frames with
ReadUntilAsync on the MLLP trailer: messages acknowledged on one connection, a negative ACK (AE)
resent, a reject (AR) not resent, a lost ACK timing out and resent on a fresh connection, an ACK
for the wrong control ID not trusted, an ACK delivered one byte at a time reassembled, and giving
up after the maximum number of attempts against a receiver that resets every connection.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Hl7MllpExample.Messages_AreAcknowledged_OnOneConnection
- Hl7MllpExample.NegativeAck_IsResent
- Hl7MllpExample.Reject_IsNotResent
- Hl7MllpExample.LostAck_TimesOut_AndIsResentOnAFreshConnection
- Hl7MllpExample.AckForTheWrongMessage_IsNotTrusted
- Hl7MllpExample.AckDribbledOutOneByteAtATime_IsReassembled
- Hl7MllpExample.ReceiverThatResetsEveryConnection_GivesUpAfterMaxAttempts
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: HTTP API client
STATEMENT: >>>
The HTTP API example shall demonstrate an HttpClient-based client: the expected request asserted,
503 retried then succeeding, giving up after three 503 responses, a truncated body and a garbage
status line reported as errors, a server that never answers hitting HttpClient.Timeout, and a
byte-at-a-time response still parsed.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- HttpApiExample.ReturnsForecast_AndSendsTheExpectedRequest
- HttpApiExample.RetriesServiceUnavailable_ThenSucceeds
- HttpApiExample.GivesUpAfterThreeUnavailableResponses
- HttpApiExample.TruncatedBody_IsAnError
- HttpApiExample.GarbageStatusLine_IsAnError
- HttpApiExample.ServerThatNeverAnswers_HitsHttpClientTimeout
- HttpApiExample.ByteAtATimeResponse_IsStillParsed
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: IMAP mailbox poller
STATEMENT: >>>
The IMAP example shall demonstrate a MailKit poller against a fake IMAPS server: unseen messages
handled then flagged seen with the password kept out of the transcript, at-least-once processing
when the connection drops mid-FETCH or the handler fails, a wrong password reported as an
authentication error, a locked mailbox (NO INUSE) reported without touching anything, and a BYE
mid-session reported as an error rather than an empty inbox.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ImapExample.UnseenMessages_AreHandled_ThenFlaggedSeen
- ImapExample.ConnectionDroppedMidFetch_LeavesTheMessageUnseen_ForTheNextPoll
- ImapExample.FailingHandler_LeavesTheMessageUnseen
- ImapExample.WrongPassword_IsAnAuthenticationError
- ImapExample.LockedMailbox_IsReported_AndNothingIsTouched
- ImapExample.ServerShuttingDown_MidSession_IsAnError_NotAnEmptyInbox
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SCPI instrument
STATEMENT: >>>
The instrument example shall demonstrate a SCPI multimeter client against a LineResponder with
LF line endings and a live log to ITestOutputHelper: identify and measure, an overload reading
parsed, a garbled reading rejected, and a fault matrix (none, 1-byte fragments, latency, connect
delay, latency beyond the timeout, disconnect and reset mid-reply) in which each case either
works or fails cleanly as expected.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- InstrumentExample.IdentifiesAndMeasures
- InstrumentExample.OverloadReading_IsParsedAsRealInstrumentsSendIt
- InstrumentExample.GarbledReading_IsRejected
- InstrumentExample.FaultMatrix_EitherWorksOrFailsCleanly
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Memcached client
STATEMENT: >>>
The memcached example shall demonstrate a working fake with mixed line and exact-length framing:
a set then get checked against a golden transcript, and values containing the protocol
terminator surviving because the length governs framing.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- MemcachedExample.SetThenGet_GoldenTranscript
- MemcachedExample.ValuesContainingTheTerminator_SurviveBecauseTheLengthGovernsFraming
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SOCKS5 and HTTP CONNECT proxies
STATEMENT: >>>
The proxy example shall demonstrate HttpClient through a relaying fake proxy: SOCKS5 tunnelling
with the proxy resolving the name, SOCKS5 with credentials and with wrong credentials, a
destination refused by policy never reached, HTTP CONNECT tunnelling TLS and answering a 407
challenge, an unreachable destination reported as 502, and a tunnel cut mid-response failing.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProxyExample.Socks5_TunnelsTheRequest_AndTheProxyResolvesTheName
- ProxyExample.Socks5_WithCredentials
- ProxyExample.Socks5_WrongCredentials_Fail
- ProxyExample.Socks5_DestinationRefusedByPolicy_Fails
- ProxyExample.HttpConnect_TunnelsTls_AndAnswersTheCredentialChallenge
- ProxyExample.HttpConnect_UnreachableDestination_Is502
- ProxyExample.ProxyCuttingTheTunnelMidResponse_Fails
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Retries by connection ID
STATEMENT: >>>
The resilience examples shall demonstrate a quote client recovering from resets on its first two
connections and giving up after three attempts.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RetryExample.RecoversFromTwoResets
- RetryExample.GivesUpAfterThreeAttempts
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: TLS certificate pinning
STATEMENT: >>>
The resilience examples shall demonstrate certificate pinning against TlsOptions.SelfSigned:
the pinned certificate accepted and any other certificate rejected with AuthenticationException.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TlsPinningExample.AcceptsThePinnedCertificate
- TlsPinningExample.RejectsAnyOtherCertificate
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Length-prefixed binary protocol
STATEMENT: >>>
The resilience examples shall demonstrate a length-prefixed binary protocol parsed with
ReadExactlyAsync: a round trip, a frame delivered one byte at a time reassembled, a truncated
frame reported as end of stream, and a length prefix corrupted by TransformWrite rejected before
allocating.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- BinaryProtocolExample.RoundTrip
- BinaryProtocolExample.ReassemblesAFrameDeliveredOneByteAtATime
- BinaryProtocolExample.TruncatedFrame_IsEndOfStream
- BinaryProtocolExample.InsaneLengthPrefix_IsRejectedBeforeAllocating
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SFTP report publisher
STATEMENT: >>>
The SFTP example shall demonstrate an SSH.NET publisher against SftpServer with an in-memory file
system: publishing via a partial file then atomic rename, a failed write retried on a new
connection, a connection cut mid-upload retried without leaving a final file behind, permission
denied not retried, an impostor host refused before any credentials are sent, an unknown key
failing authentication, collecting the inbox (download then delete, and keeping the file when
the delete fails), a hung read hitting the operation timeout, and password login.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SftpExample.Publishes_ViaPartialFileThenAtomicRename
- SftpExample.FailedWrite_IsRetriedOnANewConnection
- SftpExample.ConnectionCutMidUpload_IsRetried_AndLeavesNoFinalFileBehind
- SftpExample.PermissionDenied_IsNotRetried
- SftpExample.ImpostorHost_IsRefusedBeforeAnyCredentialsAreSent
- SftpExample.UnknownKey_FailsAuthentication
- SftpExample.CollectInbox_DownloadsThenDeletes
- SftpExample.CollectInbox_DeleteFailure_KeepsTheFile
- SftpExample.HungServer_HitsTheOperationTimeout
- SftpExample.PasswordLogin_WithSshNet
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SMTP with the BCL SmtpClient and Conversation scripts
STATEMENT: >>>
The SMTP example shall demonstrate the BCL SmtpClient against Conversation scripts: a welcome mail
sent, a rejected recipient raising SmtpFailedRecipientException, and a greylisting server
surfacing a transient failure.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpExample.SendsWelcomeMail
- SmtpExample.RejectedRecipient_Throws
- SmtpExample.GreylistingServer_SurfacesTransientFailure
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SMTP with MailKit and the ready-made SmtpServer
STATEMENT: >>>
The SMTP example shall demonstrate a MailKit order notifier against the library's SmtpServer: a
confirmation sent over STARTTLS, authenticated, with the invoice attached; greylisting retried
and delivered exactly once; a connection dropped before the server accepted the message retried;
a permanent rejection not retried; and a wrong password failing without credentials sent in the
clear.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- OrderNotifierTests.Confirmation_GoesOverTls_Authenticated_WithTheInvoiceAttached
- OrderNotifierTests.Greylisting_IsRetried_AndDeliversExactlyOnce
- OrderNotifierTests.ConnectionDroppedBeforeTheServerAccepted_IsRetried
- OrderNotifierTests.PermanentRejection_IsNotRetried
- OrderNotifierTests.WrongPassword_FailsWithoutSendingCredentialsInTheClear
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: UDP telemetry
STATEMENT: >>>
The UDP telemetry example shall demonstrate syslog and StatsD senders against UdpServer: syslog
in RFC 5424 format, well-formed StatsD metrics, tolerance of seeded 40 percent packet loss, and
senders that survive a missing collector.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- UdpTelemetryExample.Syslog_UsesRfc5424Format
- UdpTelemetryExample.Metrics_AreWellFormed
- UdpTelemetryExample.Metrics_TolerateHeavyPacketLoss
- UdpTelemetryExample.Metrics_SurviveAMissingCollector
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: F# config client
STATEMENT: >>>
The F# example shall demonstrate a task-based config client tested with a LineResponder rule
table, a Conversation script for SET then GET, a reset on the first connection retried, a hung
service timing out on every attempt, a reply cut mid-line reported as an IOException rather than
a truncated value, garbage from the service treated as a protocol error and not retried, and an
FsCheck property that SET then GET round-trips any value the protocol can carry.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ConfigClientTests.rule table: GET of a known and an unknown key
- ConfigClientTests.scripted conversation: SET then GET, exactly in that order
- ConfigClientTests.a reset on the first connection is retried
- ConfigClientTests.a hung service times out on every attempt, then fails
- ConfigClientTests.a reply cut mid-line is an error, not a truncated value
- ConfigClientTests.garbage from the service is a protocol error and is not retried
- ConfigClientTests.SET then GET round-trips any value the protocol can carry
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-EX-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: F# SMTP
STATEMENT: >>>
The F# example shall demonstrate the ready-made SmtpServer from F#: a mail sent with the BCL
SmtpClient captured with its sender, recipients, subject and body, and a recipient rejected with
FailAlways surfacing as SmtpFailedRecipientException with no message captured.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpTests.the ready-made SMTP server captures the mail
- SmtpTests.a rejected recipient surfaces as SmtpFailedRecipientException
<<<

