[[SECTION]]
TITLE: RedisLite sample

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: RESP codec

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Encode and parse round trip
STATEMENT: >>>
Encoding any RESP2 value and parsing the bytes shall give back an equal value, and concatenated
values shall parse in order.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RespCodecProperties.EncodeThenParse_RoundTrips
- RespCodecProperties.Concatenated_ValuesParseInOrder
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parsing independent of fragmentation
STATEMENT: >>>
Parsing shall give the same result however the bytes are split across buffer segments, and a
strict prefix of an encoded value shall report that more data is needed without consuming
anything.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RespCodecProperties.Parse_IsIndependentOfSegmentBoundaries
- RespCodecProperties.StrictPrefix_NeedsMoreData
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Malformed input fails only with RespProtocolException
STATEMENT: >>>
Arbitrary bytes, or a valid value with a single corrupted byte, shall fail to parse only with
RespProtocolException, and each kind of malformed input shall be rejected with a reason.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RespCodecProperties.Garbage_OnlyEverFailsWithProtocolException
- RespCodecProperties.SingleByteCorruption_OnlyEverFailsWithProtocolException
- RespCodecProperties.MalformedInput_IsRejectedWithAReason
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Canonical encoding
STATEMENT: >>>
Integers shall be encoded in canonical decimal, and simple strings containing CR or LF anywhere
shall be refused.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RespCodecProperties.Integers_UseCanonicalDecimal
- RespCodecProperties.SimpleStrings_RejectLineBreaks
- MutationTargetedTests.SimpleStrings_RejectLineBreaksAnywhere
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parser resource limits
STATEMENT: >>>
The parser shall accept arrays nested exactly to RespReader.MaxDepth (64) and reject deeper
nesting, shall fail a line with no CRLF within MaxLineLength (64 KiB), shall reject a stray CR at
the start of a line, and shall not preallocate more than 1024 elements from an array length
prefix.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A hostile or corrupt server must not be able to make the client allocate gigabytes from one
length prefix.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RespCodecProperties.DeepNesting_IsRejected
- MutationTargetedTests.Nesting_ExactlyAtTheLimit_IsAccepted
- MutationTargetedTests.LineWithoutCrLf_WaitsUpToTheLimit_ThenFails
- MutationTargetedTests.StrayCarriageReturn_AtStartOfLine_IsRejected
- MutationTargetedTests.HugeArrayHeader_DoesNotPreallocate
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Value equality
STATEMENT: >>>
RESP values shall compare by value, distinguishing nil, empty and null.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- MutationTargetedTests.ValueEquality_DistinguishesNilEmptyAndNull
<<<

