[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Resilience

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-030
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Idempotent commands retried
STATEMENT: >>>
Each command in the idempotent set (PING, ECHO, GET, SET, DEL, EXISTS, TTL, PTTL, EXPIRE,
PEXPIRE, MGET, STRLEN, TYPE, KEYS, DBSIZE) shall be retried after a connection failure, up to
MaxRetries times.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ResilienceTests.IdempotentCommand_IsRetriedAfterConnectionReset
- MutationTargetedTests.IdempotentCommands_AreRetried
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-031
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Non-idempotent commands not retried once sent
STATEMENT: >>>
A non-idempotent command (such as INCRBY or PUBLISH) that may have been sent shall not be
retried after a connection failure; the caller shall get RedisConnectionException.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ResilienceTests.NonIdempotentCommand_IsNotRetriedOnceSent
- MutationTargetedTests.NonIdempotentCommands_AreNotRetried
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-032
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Failures before sending are always retried
STATEMENT: >>>
A failure while connecting or during the handshake shall be retried for any command, including
non-idempotent ones, because nothing was sent.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ResilienceTests.FailureDuringHandshake_IsRetriedEvenForNonIdempotentCommands
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-033
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Exponential backoff
STATEMENT: >>>
The delay between retry attempts shall double from RetryBackoff on each attempt.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- MutationTargetedTests.Backoff_DoublesBetweenAttempts
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-034
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Command timeouts
STATEMENT: >>>
A command that receives no reply within CommandTimeout shall fail with RedisTimeoutException
when retries are exhausted or disabled, and an idempotent command shall recover on a new
connection when retries remain.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ResilienceTests.HungServer_TimesOut_ThenRecoversOnANewConnection
- ResilienceTests.HungServer_WithoutRetries_RaisesTimeout
- ResilienceTests.SlowServer_BeyondCommandTimeout_TimesOut
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-035
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Fail closed
STATEMENT: >>>
A timeout, a protocol error or a cut connection shall poison the connection and fail every
outstanding command immediately, and the client shall open a new connection for the next
command instead of reusing it.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ResilienceTests.ConnectionCutMidReply_IsDetected
- ClientTests.MalformedReplies_AreProtocolErrors_AndTheConnectionIsReplaced
- MutationTargetedTests.ServerClosingBetweenReplies_FailsPendingCommandsImmediately
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-036
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Fragmented replies
STATEMENT: >>>
Replies delivered one byte at a time shall be reassembled.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ResilienceTests.ByteAtATimeReplies_AreReassembled
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-037
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Reset under load
STATEMENT: >>>
When the connection is reset while many callers have commands in flight, every caller shall
complete, either with a result or with a RedisLite exception.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ResilienceTests.ResetUnderLoad_AllCallersComplete
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-038
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Exception hierarchy
STATEMENT: >>>
Every failure shall surface as a RedisException subtype: RedisConnectionException for connection
failures (including a failed write), RedisTimeoutException (a RedisConnectionException) for
timeouts, RespProtocolException for malformed replies and RedisServerException for error
replies.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- MutationTargetedTests.WriteFailure_IsAConnectionException
- ResilienceTests.UnreachableServer_IsReportedAfterRetries
- Review: samples/RedisLite/Exceptions.cs
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-RL-039
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dispose fails outstanding commands
STATEMENT: >>>
Disposing the client shall fail every outstanding command.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- MutationTargetedTests.Dispose_FailsOutstandingCommands
<<<

